{"version":"1","id":"helios","handle":"helios","name":"Helios","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/2f179172377f4811ab7f35575988341b","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-6.8245,"y":5.4998,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":63,"newest_post_at":"2024-01-16T14:06:17.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2022-04-19T06:53:54.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.015873,"listicle_ratio":0.031746,"question_ratio":0.174603,"avg_read_time":5.269841,"summary_length_avg":328.68254,"title_length_avg":50.142857,"title_length_var":339.328798,"tag_entropy":3.407982,"tag_diversity":0.952381,"top_tag_share":0.174603,"avg_upvotes":2.904762,"median_upvotes":1.0,"avg_comments":0.111111,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.043478,"zero_engagement_share":0.238095,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":0.715744,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.52381,"recency_skew":0.067797},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[1.6618,2.1912],"cadence_depth":[-3.0147,-1.6618],"hype_variety":[3.6912,2.4412],"title_style":[9.5882,6.9706]},"top_tags":[["helios",41],["observability",22],["opentelemetry",20],["microservices",19],["performance",15],["devops",14],["tools",12],["architecture",12]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Automating Backend Testing in Microservices: Challenges and Solutions","Microservices testing: traditional solutions vs. modern strategies","How I made an impact in my first 100 days at Helios"],"outlier":["How we combined OpenTelemetry traces with Prometheus metrics to build a powerful alerting mechanism"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"Eww584PFM","title":"Helios is now part of Snyk!","url":"https://gethelios.dev/blog/helios-is-now-part-of-snyk/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/helios-is-now-part-of-snyk--eww584pfm","summary":"Snyk has acquired Helios, enhancing its market-leading ASPM offering and bringing runtime insights natively into its platform.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/fc9b3e2e53459379ef1be6dcf962b34b?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-01-16T14:06:17.000Z"},{"id":"OLwyHrbQN","title":"Challenges with Traditional SCA Tools","url":"https://gethelios.dev/blog/challenges-with-traditional-sca-tools/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/challenges-with-traditional-sca-tools-olwyhrbqn","summary":"Traditional SCA tools face challenges such as long lists of vulnerabilities, high number of false positives, accumulation of a backlog of vulnerabilities, and friction between development and security teams. Runtime insights can help address these challenges by reducing false positives, improving vulnerability prioritization, and reducing friction between development and security teams.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/fc525c38f5eb0a5c4b3481e5acbaf269?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-29T10:27:36.000Z"},{"id":"eZfUf9RhW","title":"The Challenges of Collecting Runtime Data","url":"https://gethelios.dev/blog/the-challenges-of-collecting-runtime-data/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-challenges-of-collecting-runtime-data-ezfuf9rhw","summary":"Collecting runtime data presents challenges such as dealing with multiple programming languages, different deployment platforms, low-friction deployment and maintenance, and integrating new data collection mechanisms without harming existing ones.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/a8b86b426a1e9520ade4ef734502ad70?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-15T07:49:08.000Z"},{"id":"6v8EH0z6i","title":"Helios Runtime for AppSec: The missing link in application security","url":"https://gethelios.dev/blog/introducing-helios-runtime-for-appsec/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/helios-runtime-for-appsec-the-missing-link-in-application-security-6v8eh0z6i","summary":"Development teams rely heavily on open-source code, creating potential vulnerabilities that need to be assessed. Traditional SCA tools lack proper vulnerability prioritization and coverage, resulting in false positives. eBPF is being used to deliver dynamic SCA tools that provide accurate insights. Helios Runtime for AppSec combines observability and security to offer essential data on vulnerabilities and their impact. It eliminates false positives and helps prioritize vulnerabilities based on their effect on the runtime application.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/25868db95afcef1f496c803c7084451a?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-02T08:11:14.000Z"},{"id":"z8RqONXWV","title":"Convergence of Observability and Security: A New Era","url":"https://gethelios.dev/blog/convergence-of-observability-and-security-a-new-era/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/convergence-of-observability-and-security-a-new-era-z8rqonxwv","summary":"Observability and security are converging to address the challenges of a fragmented and siloed approach to securing applications. By integrating observability data and consolidating security tools, organizations can gain better context, prioritize vulnerabilities, and improve incident response efforts. This convergence is benefiting DevSecOps teams and enabling a proactive approach to security.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/e37169beaf01672ce68f2834e4e02ba1?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-09-27T14:00:11.000Z"},{"id":"CA3undH7n","title":"Helios Joins the AWS Marketplace!","url":"https://gethelios.dev/blog/helios-joins-the-aws-marketplace/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/helios-joins-the-aws-marketplace--ca3undh7n","summary":"Helios, the applied observability platform for developers, is now available on the AWS Marketplace. Anyone with an AWS account can seamlessly subscribe to Helios with just a few clicks. Helios provides visibility and runtime insights for easy troubleshooting and reduced MTTR.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f26ce0cd378428d77c0406ae2757d6b9?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-09-10T13:22:46.000Z"},{"id":"kyn4vE5nU","title":"Scaling microservices: Challenges, best practices and tools","url":"https://gethelios.dev/blog/scaling-microservices/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/scaling-microservices-challenges-best-practices-and-tools-kyn4ve5nu","summary":"Microservices scalability refers to the ability of a microservices architecture to handle increasing demand without performance degradation. Scaling microservices is a known challenge in many fields, but it\u2019s particularly pertinent when scaling microservices. The Scale Cube is a model that has been around for quite some time now. It indicates methods (or approaches) by which technology platforms may be scaled.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/49c20c52a816be937e7ca3046158e718?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":6,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-08-20T11:15:14.000Z"},{"id":"8EGsT6U6w","title":"What is Observability?","url":"https://gethelios.dev/learning-center/observability/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-is-observability--8egst6u6w","summary":"Observability is the ability to gain insights into the internal state of a system by examining its external outputs. It involves collecting and analyzing telemetry data, such as logs, metrics, and distributed traces from various sources to understand how a system behaves, and performs. The future of observability holds exciting possibilities.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/eea72a4e04bdd316ea7fb68c4a840aec?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-08-16T12:22:40.000Z"},{"id":"OzCdxvcno","title":"What are Microservices?","url":"https://gethelios.dev/learning-center/what-are-microservices/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-are-microservices--ozcdxvcno","summary":"Microservices are a software architecture pattern that structures an application as a collection of small, independent, and loosely coupled services. Each service operates as its own entity that focuses on specific business functions. Microservices allow for modular development, deployment, and scalability, providing flexibility and adaptability to changing requirements.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/b6d994fa8ac00250c71fdbba4124b32f?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":10,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-08-16T12:22:24.000Z"},{"id":"JBNPeFfO8","title":"What is eBPF?","url":"https://gethelios.dev/uncategorized/what-is-ebpf/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-is-ebpf--jbnpeffo8","summary":"eBPF, or Extended Berkeley Packet Filter, is a kernel technology that has been available since Linux 4.4.4. It lets developers run programs without adding additional modules or modifying the kernel source code. EBPF has fundamentally changed how concepts like observability, security, and networking are delivered within an app.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/10b257abe27779e664b5884fe853c07e?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-08-16T12:21:46.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["shiftmag","til","permitio","javarevisited","noted"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","hamelhusain","xai","hwchase17","sama"],"similar":[{"id":"shiftmag","handle":"shiftmag","name":"ShiftMag - Insightful Engineering Content","is_squad":true,"x":-6.7278,"y":5.5685,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":221,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--IO-OIwVf--/f_auto/v1724242797/squads/shiftmag","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":1.43539,"median_upvotes":2.0,"author_present_share":0.538462,"hype_score":0.03125,"avg_read_time":4.421569,"tag_diversity":0.751131},"top_tags_preview":[["ai",52],["productivity",47],["career",33]],"v